USE NS re DB kb;

-- ============================================================================
-- Lightning Storm super garble = slot-walk effect nodes OVER-TILING because the
-- GSTA-captured node+0xDC prefix-sum cursor + tiledesc scratch are STALE/ZEROED
-- during the super freeze. CONFIRMED-BY-MEASUREMENT 2026-06-29 (A/B TA diff).
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:gsta_fx3_ab_measurement SET kind='measurement',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/_live_fx3.gsta.mcrr + _live_fx3.mirror.zcst; _fx3_gsta_quadscan.mjs / _fx3_mirror_quadscan.mjs / _fx3_slotwalk_dump.mjs / _ab_super.mjs / _desc_probe.mjs; engine walker bank03.asm loc_8c0344d4 (10325+), inner tile loop loc_8c03478e, count=u8(tiledesc[node.0xDC+rec].byte1)+1; render_frame.c submit_1244b0 + gen_walker.c r13=*(node+0xDC)*4+0x8C1F9F9C',
  note='A/B TA DIFF (the arbiter, Jaccard 0.990 = same frame): on the super frame the engine MIRROR real-TA (7200) emits 104 quads / 104 distinct TCWs = EXACTLY 1 quad per effect TCW (each a distinct lightning-bolt texture). The GSTA reconstruction (render_frame, 7212) emits 677 quads, ~29 per effect TCW = +573 excess. Excess concentrated on contiguous effect TCWs 0x88a80,0x88ac0,0x88b00,... (0x40 apart). GSTA body count explodes 5->34. The over-emit is NOT Effect-Poly (zero 0x0CED0000 nodes); it is the slot-walk satellite nodes (layer0, cat=1, gfx1=Storm c420040, bit15-set sels 0x8006..0x801d, recCount 1-8 each) each OVER-TILING. ROOT CAUSE measured by normal-vs-super comparison (_desc_probe.mjs): on a NORMAL frame node+0xDC is a distinct non-zero per-object prefix-sum (60,53,...) indexing real tiledesc entries ([8,3,0,3]=4 tiles, [16,0,0,1]=1 tile); on the SUPER frame node+0xDC reads 0 for ALL nodes and tiledesc reads a uniform stale default [8,7,k,1] (innerTileCount=8). The engine WALKER (loc_8c0344d4) inner-tile count = u8(tiledesc[*(node+0xDC)+rec].byte1)+1; with node+0xDC=0 every record mis-indexes the stale tiledesc[0..] -> 8 tiles/record -> the ~29x explosion across the screen = the tiled Storm bodies + fists. The engine itself renders fine because its own pass writes consistent +0xDC/tiledesc; the GSTA read-set snapshots them STALE during the super freeze (the engine skips/defers the +0xDC-writing geometry-prep pass loc_8c033b0a during hitstop). All three reported symptoms (tiled bodies, effect-over-HUD, HUD layer gap) reduce to this ONE cause: the +573 garbage translucent quads blanket the screen incl the HUD region.';

UPSERT source:gsta_charpass_gate_verified SET kind='measurement',
  ref='build-headless-win/flycast.exe (rebuilt 2026-06-29) MAPLECAST_VERIFY_DC=1 in-match; oracle_hook.cpp mc_oracle_charPassCapture VERIFY-DC all-16-layer scan; [CHARPASS] realBody discriminator + CHARQ_REALBODY_MIN; node+0xDC writer loc_8c033b0a = *(0x8C1F9D98)',
  note='ROOT-CAUSE REFINED + FIX VERIFIED-BY-LIVE-MEASUREMENT. MVC2 ships TWO STARTRENDERs per video frame ([CHARPASS] log): the CHARACTER pass carries the bodies (QueueRender DROPS it, single-slot) then the surviving HUD/composite pass. node+0xDC (per-object tile-descriptor cursor; writer loc_8c033b0a: node+0xDC = *(0x8C1F9D98) the running cursor) and the tiledesc table 0x8C1F9F9C are RUNTIME-REBUILT PER PASS (loc_8c0337bc resets cursor 0x8C1F9D98<-0 + rebuilds via loc_8c129728 at the start of each pass, re_kb/22). The replica capture onRenderFrame previously fired UNCONDITIONALLY on every STARTRENDER with drop-old (last-pass-wins) -> snapshotted the HUD pass, where effect nodes the HUD pass did not re-emit read STALE/zero +0xDC -> the over-tile. LIVE VERIFY (MAPLECAST_VERIFY_DC, all-layer scan, in-match): CHARACTER pass `nodes=5 effect=3 nonZeroDC=4 zeroDC=1 sampEffNode=8c27d394 cat=3 dc=57` = effect/satellite nodes carry VALID DISTINCT NON-ZERO +0xDC; the 61 HUD passes correctly skipped. (cursor9D98 reads 0 at STARTRENDER — reset for next frame — but the per-NODE +0xDC snapshot is what the walker reads, valid on the character pass.)';

UPSERT finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile SET
  statement='FIXED 2026-06-29 (verification-positive; final acceptance gate pending a live Lightning Storm capture). The super/projectile garble in the GSTA native client = the slot-walk SATELLITE effect nodes OVER-TILING because the replica read-set captured the objpool at the WRONG render pass. MVC2 ships TWO STARTRENDERs/video-frame: the CHARACTER pass (bodies; QueueRender drops it) then the HUD/composite pass. node+0xDC (per-object tile-descriptor cursor, writer loc_8c033b0a = *(0x8C1F9D98)) and the tiledesc 0x8C1F9F9C are RUNTIME-REBUILT per pass (loc_8c0337bc/loc_8c129728, re_kb/22). The replica onRenderFrame previously captured on EVERY pass with drop-old -> snapshotted the HUD pass, where effect nodes not re-emitted read +0xDC=0 -> mis-index the stale tiledesc[0..7]=8-tiles -> ~29 quads/TCW (A/B MEASURED: GSTA 677 vs engine 104, +573 excess on the lightning TCWs). THE FIX (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp mc_oracle_charPassCapture, branch feat/render-replica-live): gate the replica capture to fire onRenderFrame ONLY on the CHARACTER pass, using the SAME realBody>=CHARQ_REALBODY_MIN discriminator CHARQ uses (ta_parse+collectScreenQuads, run only when a replica client is connected via the new maplecast_replica_live::hasClients() -> zero-overhead when idle). LIVE-VERIFIED (MAPLECAST_VERIFY_DC, all-layer scan, in-match): the CHARACTER pass effect nodes carry valid non-zero +0xDC (sample cat=3 node dc=57; 4/5 nonzero), HUD passes skipped. ACCEPTANCE GATE (pending _live_fx4 + _ab_super.mjs): GSTA per-frame quad count == mirror (~104, was 677) on super-freeze frames AND no normal-frame regression. The effect-over-HUD + HUD-layer-gap symptoms are CONSEQUENCES of the +573 garbage quads and resolve with this fix. BEST TOOL = A/B TA diff (7212 vs 7200, same frame) as the gate; MAPLECAST_VERIFY_DC confirmed the pass timing live; marvelous2/re_kb-22 gave the inner-loop formula.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_charpass_gate_verified;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->routine:loc_8c033b0a;

-- finding 22 (descriptor_table_runtime_built) is the keystone: tiledesc 0x8C1F9F9C is RUNTIME-BUILT
-- PER FRAME by loc_8c129728, and node+0xDC is re-seeded from 0x8C1F9D98 each render pass (reset by
-- loc_8c0337bc). The super-freeze stale-0 read is exactly a capture BEFORE that per-frame rebuild
-- populated the effect nodes. So the server must snapshot objpool+0xDC / tiledesc AFTER loc_8c129728.
-- ============================================================================
-- 2026-06-29 CORRECTION: the "capture on the CHARACTER pass" fix (a4ddf453f) was WRONG
-- and REGRESSED the 7212 stream to black (0 FRMx). Reverted fc45c5532. MEASURED root
-- cause of the regression (TRACE-GATE on the live headless): at the rend_start_render
-- hook (mc_oracle_charPassCapture, where onRenderFrame lives) the ONLY TA pass visible
-- is the HUD/composite pass (op=573, realBody=0). The CHARACTER geometry (op=1145,
-- realBody~36) does NOT pass through this hook in a form the realBody discriminator sees
-- — it reaches serverPublish (maplecast_mirror.cpp:1804 mc_oracle_frameFlush) instead.
-- So gating onRenderFrame on realBody>=N at this hook NEVER fires -> prefix-only stream.
-- The a4ddf453f "live verification" only passed because MAPLECAST_VERIFY_DC forced the
-- block to run; the real hasClients() path never did.
--
-- CORRECTED UNDERSTANDING (live VERIFY-DC, unconditional capture, current binary):
-- at mc_oracle_charPassCapture in NORMAL play the objpool node+0xDC IS VALID for the
-- effect/satellite nodes (nonZeroDC=4/5 every frame; sample cat=3/cat=4 nodes dc=49..76).
-- So the capture POINT is fine for normal frames. The stale node+0xDC=0 is SPECIFIC to
-- the SUPER-FREEZE (hitstop) frames seen in _live_fx3, where the engine does not re-run
-- the slot-walk geometry-prep so newly-spawned lightning effect nodes never get +0xDC
-- written (=0 initial). THEREFORE the fix is NOT a server capture-timing change at this
-- hook — it must be CLIENT-SIDE in render_frame: when the resident node+0xDC is stale-0
-- on a freeze frame, the client must use its OWN per-object prefix-sum cursor for the
-- tiledesc index. OPEN: the naive client prefix-sum hit 575 not 104 offline (the
-- circular-cursor trap, re_kb/44) — solve the cursor reconstruction (advance by actual
-- emitted TILE count, not record count) and validate vs the mirror (target 104). Needs
-- a live super capture (_live_fx4) to confirm the exact freeze-frame stale state first.
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_fx3_ab_measurement;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->routine:loc_8c0344d4;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->about->finding:descriptor_table_runtime_built;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->about->finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->about->finding:gsta_effect_decode_skip_proven;

-- 2026-06-29 (v3) — TRUE ROOT CAUSE found from the ROM: sprite_id bit15 SCALE-WALKER dispatch.
UPSERT source:gsta_bit15_scale_dispatch SET kind='disassembly',
  ref='marvelous2 bank03.asm loc_8c034bea (11259) dispatcher + loc_8c034c34=0x8000 mask + loc_8c0348c8 (10800) scale walker vs loc_8c0344d4 (10218) tiling walker; A/B vs _live_fx4 (render_frame_node.mjs)',
  note='The engine per-object dispatcher loc_8c034bea reads sel=*(node+0x144) and tests sel & 0x8000 (loc_8c034c34): (sel&0x8000)==0 -> bsr loc_8c0344d4 (the MULTI-TILE body walker, for character bodies); (sel&0x8000)!=0 -> bsr loc_8c0348c8 (the SCALE walker, ONE scaled sprite per GFX2 cell record, NO inner tile loop). MEASURED on _live_fx4 fi=545: the super EFFECT nodes carry bit15-SET sels (Lightning Storm bolts sel 0x8006..0x801d); the real bodies carry bit15-CLEAR sels (Storm 0x222, Cable 0x201). render_frame routes ALL nodes through the tiling walker loc_8c0344d4, so the bit15 effect parts mis-tile (~34x) -> the phantom tiled bodies. THE REAL FIX = honor the bit15 dispatch: run loc_8c0348c8 for bit15-set sels. (The earlier "stale node+0xDC cursor reconstruction" theory was a RED HERRING on its own: even with the cursor repaired the tiling walker is the wrong path for these parts; cursor repair only matters for the bit15-CLEAR bodies whose +0xDC is also stale-0 on a freeze frame. re_kb/44.)';

UPSERT finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile SET
  statement='ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED 2026-06-29 (fix NOT yet landed — the transpiled scale walker is buggy). The super/projectile garble = render_frame routing the bit15-SET EFFECT nodes through the TILING body walker (loc_8c0344d4) instead of the engine SCALE walker (loc_8c0348c8). ENGINE TRUTH (bank03.asm loc_8c034bea, mask loc_8c034c34=0x8000): (sel & 0x8000)==0 -> tiling walker (character bodies); (sel & 0x8000)!=0 -> scale walker (ONE scaled sprite per cell record). MVC2 super/projectile effect parts carry bit15-set sels (Lightning Storm bolts 0x8006..0x801d); the engine emits 1 sprite per part (A/B _live_fx4: engine ~50-90 quads on the super-freeze frame, each effect TCW once). render_frame tiled them ~34x -> phantom bodies (GSTA 529 vs engine ~90 on fi=545). TWO sub-fixes are needed and were prototyped: (1) bit15 dispatch -> a transpiled walker_0348c8 (gen_walker_scale.py, loc_8c0348c8); (2) on a SUPER-FREEZE frame the resident node+0xDC is stale-0 for ALL nodes (hitstop skips the geometry-prep loc_8c033b0a = *(0x8C1F9D98)), so BOTH walkers also need the prefix-sum cursor repaired (resident==0 && s_running_cursor!=0 -> use s_running_cursor). STATUS: NOT LANDED. The mechanical transpile gen_walker_scale.c is WRONG — it loses the 88xxx lightning TCWs entirely (emits c1xxx/other instead), i.e. its TCW resolution does not match the engine (re_kb/44: an unvalidated mechanical port lies). The bit15-clear cursor repair DID work (obj33 Storm body nt 55->21; normal frame fi=100 unregressed at 69==mirror). NO client shipped (render_frame.c reverted to clean; deployed render_frame unchanged; 7212 stream healthy at 60 FRMx/s). REMAINING WORK: debug walker_0348c8 so it emits the SAME 88xxx effect TCWs as the engine (once each) — likely a lift error in the scale walker\'s per-record TCW/rectab-index resolution or its register setup; validate per-node vs the engine (the scale walker shares submit_1244b0, so compare its alloc_index/r13 to the engine\'s for one effect node). Acceptance gate (_live_fx4 _ab_super.mjs): fi=545->~90, fi=765->~90, fi=775->~58, fi=100 unregressed (69). Tools committed: gen_walker_scale.py/.c. Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_bit15_scale_dispatch;
RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->about->finding:atlas_coverage_and_bit15;

-- 2026-06-29 (v4) — SCALE-WALKER divergence isolated to the per-record ALLOC-INDEX (rectab index).
UPSERT source:gsta_scale_walker_index_diverge SET kind='measurement',
  ref='instrumented submit_1244b0 (MC_DBG_SUBMIT) on _live_fx4 fi=545 effect node 8c27a9e4 sel=8006; bank03.asm loc_8c0348c8 index path loc_8c034986 (10914-10945) + loc_8c0349cc (10951-10967); pools loc_8c034ab4=0x180 ab6=0x1ff ab8=0x220 aba=0x390 abc=0x1a4 abe=0x15c ac8=0x8C1F9D84',
  note='MEASURED the exact divergence of the transpiled scale walker walker_0348c8 vs the working tiling walker on the SAME effect node (8c27a9e4, sel 0x8006, 8 records). The TILING walker (which, when forced, emits the CORRECT 88xxx effect TCWs by over-tiling) computes alloc_index = arena_base(=*(0x8C1F9D94)=400) + node+0xDC + k -> 400,401,402,... (r11=valid cell ptr 0x0c509b4e, sel read OK = 0x44,0x48,...). The SCALE walker computes alloc_index via a DIFFERENT formula: r5 = *(node+0x180) + 0x220 + read.w(*(node+0x244)&0x1ff <<1); index = read.b(r5+counter) | (read.b(node+0x1a4)<<8) + 0x390. On the captured freeze frame node+0x180=0x0C565000 (a resident template, shipped non-zero), node+0x1a4=0, node+0x244=0 -> index = 0x390(912) + template_byte = 912,913,914,... Feeding 912 to gen_submit_params resolves to c1xxx/garbage, NOT the engine 88xxx. So my scale walker\'s index (912) does not match what the engine resolves to 88xxx. The lift of loc_8c034986/loc_8c0349cc is byte-faithful to the disasm (verified instruction-by-instruction), so the divergence is EITHER (a) a subtle lift error elsewhere in the 362-insn routine feeding node+0x180/0x1a4/0x244 or the r5 base, OR (b) a SHIPPED-TABLE staleness on the freeze frame (the 0x0C565000 effect rectab-template region, or idxtab[912], holds a previous-frame value), OR (c) gen_submit_params needs scale-walker-specific index handling. CANNOT disambiguate offline without the ENGINE\'s actual per-record alloc_index. NEEDS a live ASMTRACE on loc_8c0348c8 (the scale walker) during a Lightning Storm: capture, per emitted effect sprite, the engine\'s r4 -> *(r4+0)=alloc_index, r13 (cell ptr), node+0x180/0x1a4/0x244, and the resolved TCW — then diff vs my walker_0348c8 for the same node. Also confirm whether the engine alloc_index is ~400 (arena-relative, like tiling) or ~912 (the 0x390 base), which decides (a) vs (b)/(c).';

UPSERT finding:gsta_scale_walker_index_open SET
  statement='OPEN (needs live ASMTRACE on loc_8c0348c8). The bit15 SCALE-walker fix is right in principle (re_kb/50) but the transpiled walker_0348c8 resolves the WRONG rectab alloc-index for the effect records, so it emits c1xxx/garbage TCWs instead of the engine 88xxx. ISOLATED (MC_DBG_SUBMIT on _live_fx4 fi=545, node 8c27a9e4): scale-walker index = 0x390(912)+template_byte via node+0x180(=0x0C565000)/+0x1a4(=0)/+0x244(=0); the tiling walker (correct 88xxx) uses arena_base(400)+node+0xDC+k. The scale index formula is lifted byte-faithfully from loc_8c034986/loc_8c0349cc, so the bug is either a lift error elsewhere feeding node+0x180/0x1a4 or the r5 base, OR a freeze-frame staleness in the 0x0C565000 template / idxtab[912], OR a gen_submit_params index-handling gap. REQUEST: live ASMTRACE on loc_8c0348c8 during a Lightning Storm capturing per effect sprite the engine r4->*(r4+0) alloc_index + r13 + node+0x180/0x1a4/0x244 + resolved TCW, to diff vs walker_0348c8 and decide arena-relative(~400) vs 0x390-base(~912). NO client shipped; deployed render_frame clean; 7212 healthy at 60 FRMx/s. Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_scale_walker_index_open->cites->source:gsta_scale_walker_index_diverge;
RELATE finding:gsta_scale_walker_index_open->about->finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile;

-- 2026-06-29 (v5) — LIVE ASMTRACE on loc_8c0348c8 (PC 0x8C034BA4) DECIDED the mechanism.
UPSERT source:gsta_scale_template_stale_proven SET kind='measurement',
  ref='live ASMTRACE PC 0x8C034BA4 scaleidx (mc_scaleidx.log, 3790 fires/54 super vframes); _live_fx4 wire-region check; bank13.asm loc_8c135594 (template bases) + loc_8c1355b4 (ends); gen_submit_params.c read_template (idxtab=u16!)',
  note='DECISIVE: the engine scale walker per-record alloc_index (r15+0xC) = 0x3CC..0x432, derived from read.b(*(node+0x180)+0x220+ctr) where node+0x180=0x0C565000 is a PER-CHARACTER effect display-list TEMPLATE (bank13.asm: 7 char slots, each a 0x3000 arena 0x0C565000..0x0C568000 etc). The engine REBUILDS this template every frame; the GSTA wire only rode the once-shipped static 16MB RAM image, so offline render reads STALE bytes (00,01,02..) -> index 912 -> wrong TCW. CONFIRMED the template region is covered ONLY by static ram16 (NOT any per-frame dynamic region) in _live_fx4. FIX = ship the 7 effect-template arenas per-frame (maplecast_replica_live.cpp "efxtmpl", additive read-set, headless rebuilt 16:07; 24 dyn regions; stream verified 59.3 FRMx/s). ALSO corrected a manual-analysis error: idxtab entries are u16 (gen_submit_params read_template: r16u(idxtab+idx*2)), NOT u32 — so prior offline idxtab resolution was wrong. The bit15 dispatch + scale walker (gen_walker_scale.c) + bit15-clear cursor-repair are re-applied in render_frame.c; fi=100 unregressed (69==69). VALIDATION REQUIRES A FRESH super capture (the _live_fx4 template is stale); offline injection of a right-range index alone did NOT fix it (idxtab[effect-range] also resolves wrong in the stale capture), so the live efxtmpl + live idxtab/rectab of a fresh capture is the discriminator.';

UPSERT finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile SET
  statement='FIX IMPLEMENTED 2026-06-29, pending fresh-capture validation. Root cause = render_frame ran the tiling walker for the bit15 EFFECT nodes (must use the SCALE walker loc_8c0348c8), AND the scale walker\'s per-record alloc-index reads a per-character effect TEMPLATE (node+0x180=0x0C565000-family, bank13.asm) that the engine REBUILDS every frame but the GSTA wire only shipped ONCE (static ram16) -> stale -> wrong index -> wrong (c1xxx) TCW. LIVE ASMTRACE (PC 0x8C034BA4) proved the engine index=0x3CC..0x432 derives from live non-zero template bytes that DIFFER from the prefix snapshot. FIX (3 parts, all applied): (1) bit15 dispatch -> walker_0348c8 (gen_walker_scale.py/.c); (2) ship the 7 effect-template arenas per-frame (maplecast_replica_live.cpp D(0x8C565000..,0x3000,"efxtmpl") — additive read-set, NOT the capture-gate revert; headless rebuilt 16:07, 24 dyn regions, stream 59.3 FRMx/s HEALTHY); (3) bit15-clear super-freeze cursor-repair (resident node+0xDC stale-0 -> s_running_cursor). fi=100 unregressed (69==69). The _live_fx4 capture predates the read-set fix (its template is stale), so a FRESH super capture is needed to validate the effect TCWs (then fi=545->~90, 765->~90, 775->~58). Probe armed (scaleidx PC 0x8C034BA4, effect-scoped, stream-safe) on the running headless to capture the engine ground-truth alloc_index for the diff if it still fails. Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_scale_template_stale_proven;

-- 2026-06-29 (v6) — FRESH CAPTURE (_live_fx5, read-set-fix headless) RIGOROUS A/B.
UPSERT source:gsta_fx5_validation SET kind='measurement',
  ref='_live_fx5.gsta.mcrr + _live_fx5.mirror.zcst (read-set-fix headless, live efxtmpl) + mc_scaleidx2.log (engine alloc_index ground truth); render_frame_node (bit15 dispatch + scale walker + cursor repair)',
  note='RIGOROUS VALIDATION RESULT — PARTIAL. WINS (confirmed): (1) the 34x over-tile is GONE — effect TCWs now emit 1x each (was 88xxx@34 on _live_fx4); (2) NO regression — non-effect frames match the mirror at Jaccard=1.000 (fi=300 44==44, fi=340 96==96); (3) the scale walker\'s alloc_index is now CORRECT — with the live efxtmpl shipped, the scale-subset indices (>=912) are 978..1074, ALL within the engine\'s measured 972..1074 (mc_scaleidx2.log), 77 distinct, matching the engine range. RESIDUAL (real, not skew): the effect parts resolve to the WRONG TEXTURE. For the engine\'s index 1005 (node 8C283914, the trace ground truth), MY shipped idxtab resolves idxtab[1005]=872 -> rectab[872].tcw=c1e00 (a c1xxx BODY texture), but the engine rendered an effect (89/8a) TCW. MEASURED: idxtab[1005]=872 is STATIC across ALL frames incl non-super (never the effect value); rectab DOES contain the effect textures (192 entries with 89-8b TCW at fi=235); the idxtab/rectab POINTERS (*0x8C2DAD3C/4C) are static. So the EFFECT-RANGE idxtab entries (idxtab[972..1074]) are STALE in the wire — they hold body-entry values, not the live effect entries the engine writes TRANSIENTLY during the character-pass submit and reverts before the HUD-pass capture (the same character-pass-transient class as the original +0xDC, but now for idxtab). GSTA emits fabricated effect TCWs (e.g. 8abc0,8ac00,8b000 — present in 0/1083 mirror frames) because idxtab maps the (correct) effect indices to (stale body) rectab entries. NEEDS: capture the idxtab effect-range entries at the CHARACTER pass (when the effect display list is live) — a targeted char-pass snapshot of just idxtab/rectab, NOT the whole-capture pass-gate that broke the stream. Or resolve the effect rectab entry without the transient idxtab (the rectab has the effect textures; the missing piece is the index->rectab-entry mapping for effects).';

UPSERT finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile SET
  statement='OVER-TILE FIXED + NO REGRESSION (validated on fresh _live_fx5); EFFECT-TEXTURE residual remains. WINS (CONFIRMED-BY-MEASUREMENT on _live_fx5, read-set-fix headless): (1) the 34x effect over-tile is GONE (effect TCWs now 1x each); (2) NO regression — non-effect frames match the mirror at Jaccard=1.000; (3) the scale walker alloc_index is now CORRECT (live efxtmpl: scale indices 978..1074 all within engine 972..1074 per mc_scaleidx2.log). RESIDUAL (real, not frame-skew): effect parts resolve to the WRONG TEXTURE — for engine index 1005, MY shipped idxtab[1005]=872 -> rectab[872]=c1e00 (a BODY texture), but the engine rendered an effect (89/8a) TCW. The effect-range idxtab entries (idxtab[972..1074]) are STALE in the wire: idxtab[1005]=872 is static across ALL frames (never the effect value), while rectab DOES hold the effect textures (192 effect entries). So the idxtab effect entries are CHARACTER-PASS-TRANSIENT — the engine writes them during the char-pass submit and reverts before the HUD-pass capture (same class as the original +0xDC staleness). NEXT STEP (needs another capture): snapshot idxtab/rectab effect range at the CHARACTER pass (targeted, NOT the whole-capture pass-gate that broke the stream), OR derive the effect index->rectab-entry mapping another way. DO NOT SHIP (re_kb/44): the over-tile garble would be replaced by wrong-texture effects (body parts at effect positions). The 3 fix parts (read-set efxtmpl, bit15 dispatch, cursor repair) are CORRECT and committed; the idxtab-effect-staleness is the last layer. Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_fx5_validation;

-- 2026-06-29 (v7) — RESOLVED. The super/projectile garble is FIXED end-to-end, validated
-- offline against the 7200 mirror ground truth on _live_fx6 (no further super needed).
UPSERT source:gsta_effect_idxtab_remap_validated SET kind='measurement',
  ref='_live_fx6.gsta.mcrr + _live_fx6.mirror.zcst + snap3.err (serverPublish-too-late verdict) + mc_scaleidx_fx6.log (engine alloc_index 972..1074); render_frame.c effect remap',
  note='FINAL FIX validated. (1) serverPublish char-pass snapshot verdict: idxtab[1005]=872 tcw=c1e00 on all 3744 fires incl the super -> serverPublish runs after BOTH render walks, effect idxtab already reverted (too late). (2) OFFLINE CLOSE: the fresh rectab contains the effect textures in a CONTIGUOUS block (effect-band 0x89000..0x8bfff, entries 415..606, MEASURED stable across all super frames); the engine maps the contiguous effect index range 1:1 onto it. CORRECT entry = effect_block_start + (alloc_index - idx_base); effect_block_start from a rectab effect-band scan, idx_base = match-global min scale-walker alloc_index. (3) render_frame.c applies this remap to the SCALE walker submit only (bit15 quads); body quads untouched. (4) VALIDATED vs 7200 mirror: 103/103 reconstructed effect TCWs are REAL engine textures in the mirror, 0 fabricated, across all super frames; GSTA quad count tracks mirror (87 vs 92, 117 vs 109); residual Jaccard ~0.89 is frame-skew (body path caps at the same ~0.91; fabricated=0 proves textures right). NO regression: normal frames have 0 bit15 nodes -> remap is a strict no-op (fi=100/50 untouched). Web render_frame.wasm + native build/flycast.exe (gsta_render_frame.c amalgamation now #includes gen_walker_scale.c) rebuilt.';

UPSERT finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile SET
  statement='RESOLVED 2026-06-29. The MVC2 super/projectile (Lightning Storm) garble is fixed end-to-end, validated offline vs the 7200 mirror ground truth (re_kb/44 satisfied; no remaining super needed). THREE root causes, all fixed: (1) render_frame ran the TILING body walker for bit15 EFFECT nodes -> ~34x over-tile (the phantom tiled bodies); fix = honor the engine bit15 dispatch loc_8c034bea & 0x8000 -> the SCALE walker loc_8c0348c8 (gen_walker_scale.c). (2) the scale walker per-record alloc-index reads a per-character effect TEMPLATE (node+0x180=0x0C565000-family) the engine rebuilds each frame but the wire shipped ONCE -> stale index; fix = ship the 7 efxtmpl arenas per-frame (maplecast_replica_live.cpp, additive read-set). (3) the idxtab effect entries (alloc_index 972..1074) are character-pass-transient and the wire ships them stale -> effect parts resolved the wrong (body) texture; fix = CLIENT-side remap in render_frame: effect entry = effect_block_start + (alloc_index - idx_base), both derived from the wire (rectab effect-band scan + match-global min effect alloc_index). Plus a bit15-CLEAR super-freeze cursor repair (resident node+0xDC stale-0 -> s_running_cursor). VALIDATED vs the mirror on _live_fx6: over-tile GONE (effect TCWs 1x each), effect textures RIGHT (103/103 reconstructed effect TCWs are real engine textures in the mirror, 0 fabricated, all super frames), GSTA quad count ~= mirror, NO normal-frame regression (remap is a no-op when no bit15 nodes). The residual ~0.89 Jaccard is frame-skew between the two unsynchronized capture streams, not a render bug (fabricated=0). Web + native client rebuilt; user does the final visual verify. The serverPublish char-pass snapshot infra (7e2c2a649) is superseded by the client remap and left inert. Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-29';

RELATE finding:gsta_super_effect_overtile->cites->source:gsta_effect_idxtab_remap_validated;
